            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "Calculate Pearson’s correlation coefficient $r$, correct to 4 decimal places.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$r\\approx0.9918$",
              "worked": "Enter the years in A2:A10 and the populations in B2:B10. Using =CORREL(A2:A10,B2:B10) gives $r=0.991798951\\ldots\\approx0.9918$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 12
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q3-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "Describe the strength and direction.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Strong positive.",
              "worked": "$r\\approx0.9918$ is positive and close to 1, so the association is strong and positive.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 12
          },
          {
            "id": "p45-q3-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "Find the equation of the line of best fit $y=mx+c$, where $x$ is the year and $y$ is population in millions. Round $m$ to 3 decimal places and $c$ to 2 decimal places.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y\\approx0.203x-386.87$",
              "worked": "Create a scatter chart with year on the horizontal axis and population on the vertical axis. Add a linear trendline and display its equation. The spreadsheet gives $m=0.203016666\\ldots$ and $c=-386.869183333\\ldots$, so $y\\approx0.203x-386.87$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p45-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Interpret the gradient and $y$-intercept.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The model estimates an increase of 0.203 million people per year. The intercept −386.87 million is the formal model value at $x=0$; it has no realistic population interpretation.",
          "worked": "The gradient is $0.203$ million people per year, so the fitted model estimates an average annual population increase of about 203 000 people over the observed period. At $x=0$, the model gives $y=-386.87$ million. This is far outside 1931–2011 and is negative, so the intercept is not a meaningful prediction of Australia's population.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
